  "notes": "Native Rust research screen on shared six-slot capture-bank quiet-drop rules, not Classic. Candidate has no node cap; Native process has a 30-second failure watchdog, not a search budget; search explicitly uses candidateMillis. Fairy has 100ms per move, one thread, 16MiB hash, NNUE off. Candidate and Fairy budgets explicitly recorded in manifest; native IPC overhead is included in actual candidate timing. Selective algorithms differ; results are not universal strength evidence. Fixed colors and recorded schedule seeds (native ties deterministic); repeated starts are correlated. Root legal parity checked every move; full history supplied. Requested depth counts plies, quiescence/reductions make this selective search. Proven mates may finish before requested depth. Every attempt is retained, not just successful screens. A successful screen requires a separate frozen confirmation schedule."
